Unreleased
==========

* Unquoted CIF data values `?' (unknown) and `.' (not applicable) are now
represented by the `str' subclasses `StarUnknown' and `StarInapplicable'
(exported from the CifFile module), so they can be distinguished from quoted
text values of `?' and `.' and from empty text.  Output routines reproduce
the original form (bare `?'/`.' for the special values, quoted otherwise),
so a read-write-read round trip restores each value exactly, in both
dataname-value pairs and loops.

* DDLm mandatory-item checking (`check_mandatory_items') now treats a
mandatory item whose values are all unknown (`?') as not submitted, while
an inapplicable (`.') value counts as an explicit declaration and is not
reported as missing.  DDLm validity information is now also read from
`_dictionary_valid.application', matching current DDLm dictionaries.

